224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (North Sikkim is one of the most beautiful and untouched regions of India, renowned for its pristine natural beauty and serene environment. The region is characterized by lush green valleys, snow-capped mountains, and a rich cultural heritage. Lachung, a charming village in North Sikkim, serves as the gateway to the breathtaking Yumthang Valley, known as the Valley of Flowers. This valley is famous for its vibrant floral landscape and hot springs with therapeutic properties. Zero Point, located at an altitude of 16,000 feet, offers an unmatched view of the snow-covered Himalayas and gives a sense of touching the sky. Nathula Pass, situated at an altitude of 14,140 feet, is a strategic mountain pass on the Indo-China border. It holds significant historical and geopolitical importance and is known for its stunning landscapes and the Indo-China border trading post. The pass is accessible only to Indian nationals and requires a special permit due to its sensitive location.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
